# Manager view — current scope

The **Manager view** (`ManagerView.html`, `manager-view/`) is an active product surface. **Do not remove, revert, or “baseline-restore”** features the user has designed unless they explicitly ask.

## Main tabs (all in scope)

| Tab | Purpose |
|-----|---------|
| Full Team Roster | Org-wide IM list/card views, regional filter, notes |
| Deal Assignment Review | Queue, rotation alerts/removals, IM eligibility |
| **Project Management** | Read-only rollup — **retain as implemented** |
| Reporting | Charts, date range, Apply vs Refresh data |

## Project Management (Manager) — retain as designed

These are **intentional** and must stay unless the user requests changes:

- `manager-view/manager-projects.js`
- `ManagerView.html`: `tab-projects`, `view-projects`, sub-tabs **Project Roster** / **My Projects**
- Imports: `shared/projects-data.js`, `shared/lead-view.css` (roster table styling)
- `manager-view/manager-view.js`: `renderManagerProjects()`, `ProjectsData` / `countRegionalProjects()`, project tab in `switchSubTab` / `setTZFilter` / `reloadFromSharedStore`

**Manager PM is narrower than Team Lead** (by design):

- **Regional View** filter applies; **T1 IMs excluded** from contributor roster (`ProjectsData.canIMBeProjectContributor`)
- **Project Roster**: IM sections only (no territory-leads table)
- **My Projects**: sponsor list for `TeamData.MANAGER_SPONSOR` — view only, no New Project / edit modals

Do **not** port Lead-only flows (new project form, edit modal, contributor editing) into Manager unless the user explicitly asks.

## Reporting (Manager)

- `manager-view/reporting.js`, `reporting-data.js`, `reporting.css`
- Charts use mock/seeded HubSpot-style metrics in `reporting-data.js`; roster/deals from `TeamData` / `ICSync`
- **Apply** = date range + charts from memory; **Refresh data** = reload roster + metrics + charts
- Reporting refreshes on tab open / **Refresh data**, not on every cross-view edit while Reporting is active
- Layout/prefs keys: `imworkdash_reporting_layout_v3`, `imworkdash_reporting_prefs_v2`

## Team Lead Project Management (separate, more robust)

`LeadView.html`, `shared/lead-view.js`, `shared/lead-view.css`, `shared/projects-data.js` — full territory PM (roster, new/edit project, sponsors). Changes there **do not** require matching Manager CRUD; only shared data/contracts (`ProjectsData`, `TeamData`) when behavior must stay consistent.

## Shared data & shell

- Roster/sync: `shared/team-data.js`, `shared/ic-sync.js`, `shared/view-sync.js`
- Unified entry: `index.html` (role iframes); hidden frames defer sync until active

## Do not do unless asked

- Delete `manager-projects.js` or strip the Project Management tab
- Run `git restore ManagerView.html manager-view/` to wipe current Manager work
- Re-apply old “5/29 only / no Manager PM” restrictions from prior rule versions
- Assume Reporting metrics are live HubSpot API data

## When editing Manager files

Match existing patterns in `manager-view.js` and sibling modules: globals for roster/assignment onclick handlers, `ManagerProjects` / `ManagerReporting` IIFEs for namespaced APIs, regional filter via `currentTZ`, embed-aware refresh via `IMWorkdashViewSync` / `isEmbedFrameActive()`.
